119
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:20,420
So what I do is I require, I ask my dev leads to give estimates

120
00:06:20,420 --> 00:06:21,540
on everything they deliver.

121
00:06:21,540 --> 00:06:23,060
When is this project going to be done?

122
00:06:26,350 --> 00:06:28,750
And again, predicting the future is impossible,

123
00:06:28,750 --> 00:06:30,190
but we're trying to give the best guess.

124
00:06:30,190 --> 00:06:31,630
So I had to use confidence levels.

125
00:06:31,630 --> 00:06:34,190
So give me a date that you have a 50% confidence in.

126
00:06:34,190 --> 00:06:38,480
And what I found in years of experimenting is that 50% is a sweet spot

127
00:06:38,480 --> 00:06:41,920
between putting some decent planning into place

128
00:06:41,920 --> 00:06:43,520
and completely guessing on what you're doing.

129
00:06:47,980 --> 00:06:51,020
I go over this stuff weekly with the leads.

130
00:06:51,020 --> 00:06:55,980
And what I track is the day their initial estimate date

131
00:06:55,980 --> 00:06:57,980
and the actual date they deliver.

132
00:06:57,980 --> 00:07:01,500
So I can get deltas between the date something's actually done

133
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:03,020
